>> title: Home Fries
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: potatoes, breakfast, skillet, bacon fat, stovetop
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: homefries, home fried potatoes, country fries, cottage fries, breakfast potatoes, diner potatoes
>> pairs-with: homemade-ketchup
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> step.1: simmer whole 12 min, until a knife just enters
>> step.2: drain, cool 10 min, cut in 3/4-in dice
>> step.3: brown cut faces down 8 min, undisturbed
>> step.4: turn in the onion and pepper, brown 6 min
>> step.5: season off the heat

Simmer @Yukon Gold potatoes{2%lb}(900 g; whole, skin on) in @water{3%qt}(2.8 L) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}(18 g) ~simmer{12%min}, until a knife enters the widest part with a little resistance left in it.

Drain @&(~1)potatoes{} and ~cool{10%min}, then cut them into 3/4-in dice.

Brown @&(~1)diced potatoes{} in @bacon fat{3%Tbs}(40 g) in a #cast-iron skillet{} over medium-high heat ~fry{8%min}, cut faces down and left alone, until one side carries a solid crust.

Turn @&(~1)browning potatoes{} with @yellow onion{1%medium}(diced) and @green bell pepper{1}(diced), and keep them moving ~fry{6%min}.

Season @&(~1)home fries{} off the heat with @sweet paprika{1%tsp}(2 g), @kosher salt{1%tsp}(6 g) and @coarse black pepper{1/2%tsp}(1 g).
